      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:180:6",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) إِنَّ أَهْلَ مَكَّةَ أَنْكَرُوا عَلَيْكَ أَنَّكَ ذَبَحْتَ هَدْيَكَ فِي مَنْزِلِكَ بِمَكَّةَ فَقَالَ إِنَّ مَكَّةَ كُلَّهَا مَنْحَرٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya Bin Ammar who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘The people of Makkah are denying upon you<sup>asws</sup> that you<sup>asws</sup> slaughtered your<sup>asws</sup> offering in your<sup>asws</sup> house in Makkah’. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Verily Makkah, the whole of it, is a place for sacrifice’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Ammar who has said the following: “I once said to abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, that people of Makkah disliked my slaughtering the offering in my lodging in Makkah. He (the Imam) said, ‘All of Makkah is the place to slaughter offerings.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
